-1$ will give only one solution to the equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110612 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "637d4fe0-abb6-5050-a541-f132e78f9b8a" :knowledge-point/title "Cases When the Perfect Square is Isolated"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24859fd2-c1b2-5831-8e51-fb1466c128e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533231} {:answer/id #uuid "855b1c7e-4914-5f65-94b2-e15147369927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533453} {:answer/id #uuid "f0cad8d3-af30-578b-91c1-ab1f9fb13ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533730} {:answer/id #uuid "f263fd6b-0416-5c5a-a3b8-d6abab2d6179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533735} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3dee97-f98b-5e4b-b74d-89fe2dc202cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0cad8d3-af30-578b-91c1-ab1f9fb13ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533730} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd233f5-e9c5-585c-aae5-bf5e3fead6e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4515a99f-af9e-5afd-8162-572a1dd1a9d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-44355" :question/problem "Solve $(2q+1)^{2}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2q+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{(2q+1)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |2q+1| & =0 \\\\ 2q+1 & =0 \\\\ 2q & =-1 \\\\ q & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
